description:
Root Cause: In responder.rs process_message_1() at lines 254-265, the C_I parsing logic extracts the connection identifier value but never checks for trailing bytes afterward. When C_I is encoded as a 1-byte bstr (0x41 + value = 2 bytes), the parser extracts rest[1] as C_I but ignores any remaining bytes in rest[2..]. The test pushes an extra byte to message_1 (simulating unsupported EAD_1), but the parser silently ignores it and returns Ok instead of Err(InvalidMessage).

Affected Test: rejects_unconfigured_ead_trailing_items_and_parses_suite_error

Location: /Volumes/Attic/Desktop/Projects/crates/oscore/src/edhoc/responder.rs:254-265

Suggested Fix: After parsing C_I (around line 265), add a check to reject trailing bytes since EAD is not supported:

let c_i_len = if rest[0] <= 23 { 1 } else { 2 };
// Reject trailing items (EAD_1) - not configured/supported
if rest.len() > c_i_len {
    return Err(EdhocError::InvalidMessage);
}

This ensures any bytes after the C_I encoding are rejected as InvalidMessage, which is the expected behavior when EAD processing is not configured.

Error Type: Missing input validation - security-relevant: silently ignoring unexpected message content could mask protocol violations
